  "body": "Released: 2026-09-16\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Upgrades recognize stopped daemons even when another process has reused\n  their process ID.\n- Daemon status no longer requests a restart solely because another shell has\n  different locale, temporary-directory, or session settings.\n- Windows manual upgrades and semantic-runtime repairs record completion\n  before restarting background indexing. Resume preserves the installed\n  environment and data-root path.\n- Windows scheduled tasks wait for fresh daemon ownership when process IDs\n  are reused.\n- Hosted installers accept supported existing semantic and named-source settings.\n\n### Commits and PRs\n\n- Source commit: [31109e1d](https://github.com/ctxrs/ctx/commit/31109e1d4fcb8dc522a70a24061c389ab44e42ef).\n- Full diff: [v1.4.9...31109e1d](https://github.com/ctxrs/ctx/compare/v1.4.9...31109e1d4fcb8dc522a70a24061c389ab44e42ef).\n- [#1006](https://github.com/ctxrs/ctx/pull/1006) — restore daemon availability after upgrades and shell changes.\n- [#1007](https://github.com/ctxrs/ctx/pull/1007) — preserve Windows task ownership across upgrades.\n- [#1008](https://github.com/ctxrs/ctx/pull/1008) — prepare the 1.4.10 patch release.\n"
}
